Phase P0 — bidirectionality verification log (#140 arc)
=======================================================

Method: each new production behaviour is proven bidirectionally — the pinning
test PASSES on committed code, a compiling MUTATION of the committed code makes
that test FAIL for the RIGHT reason (a real value/behaviour diff, not a
compile/crash artifact), and RESTORE returns the suite to green. Mutations were
applied to committed code (all work committed first) and reverted with
`git checkout`; targets addressed by content (capture-then-grep), never line
numbers. Every mutant compiled (tsc-valid) — a mutant that fails to compile
proves nothing.

All commands run from the worktree root:
  /home/subzerodev/workspace/satisfactory-foundry/.worktrees/phase-p0

Baseline before P0: 1165 tests passing. After P0: 1177 tests passing (+12).

